    "note": "triage cost is per AUTO-ACTED comment; the encoder needs 1 amortizable small-encoder embed, the LLM pipeline needs 1 12B forward pass. Human-reviewed comments cost human time regardless of method -- which is exactly what the f-fraction quantifies."
  },
  "headline": "On Kumar's balanced test fold, to reach a TOTAL-SYSTEM quality bar of precision>=90% AND recall>=90%, a frozen-e5 triage ranker escalates only 40.8% of comments to humans, versus 75.3% for the best LLM-only pipeline (llm_random); the cheap encoder saves 46% of human-review hours (clustered-bootstrap median 47%, 95% CI [43%, 51%]). The encoder's CONTINUOUS per-sub score lets it rank exactly the boundary cases to escalate; the LLM is binary at the decision and its 1..5 rating is ~64% missing and degenerate on keep, so it cannot target edge cases -- it games a precision-only target by being low-recall (catches only ~57% of true removals), but on the joint bar that conservatism costs human hours. A cheap encoder both triages and surfaces the right edge cases."
}